=1 312 16
+    If the exception is a bus error, the bus error processing routine is
+    called. If the previous mode is kernel, then the exception dispatcher is
+    called directly to process the exception. Otherwise the exception record,
+    exception frame, and trap frame contents are copied to the user mode
+    stack. The contents of the exception frame and trap are then modified
+    such that when control is returned, execution will commense in user mode
+    in a routine which will call the exception dispatcher.
